Incompatible types in bitwise operation.
Hint: the operands of a bitwise operator must either:
	1. both be of type boolean or Boolean, or
	2. both be of an integral type (i.e. byte, short, int, long, or char), or a reference type that can be unboxed to an integral type (i.e. Byte, Short, Integer, Long, or Character).
